# The build context for software_factory/Dockerfile.
#
# The absence of this file is a real defect, not an oversight. `target/` here was 2.6GB on a
# developer machine, and because `COPY . .` was unrestricted, that entire directory was sent
# to the Docker daemon on every build and then copied into the image. The first build of this
# project took over four minutes largely because of a build cache being uploaded.
#
# Ignore the build output and the VCS metadata. `Cargo.lock` is deliberately NOT ignored:
# it is the reason this image is reproducible, and excluding it would reintroduce the exact
# defect that let the image resolve a different dependency graph than the tested one.
target/
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
*.md
k8s/
scripts/
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
